  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1250 AM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nThe passing front will also bring a stark cooldown for all areas \nby Sunday, with temperatures running 10-20 degrees cooler compared\nto Saturday. In fact, there is medium-high confidence that \nportions of northwestern Oklahoma fail to warm out of the 40s on \nSunday afternoon.\n\nMost of Sunday and Monday will be dry with generally cooler (yet \nseasonable) temperatures across the area. The next weather system\nof interest looks to arrive sometime on Tuesday, with low \npotential for precipitation along with a reinforcing cooler \nairmass. \n\nWhile occasional deterministic model runs depict some chance for \nwintry precipitation during the midweek, this remains highly \nuncertain, and the subtropical origins of the upper system and \nlack of preceding cold airmass do not given much confidence in \nthis solution becoming reality.\n\nUngar",
